{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work","id":987569,"title":"How do Garou Families work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-14T20:05:55-07:00","id":987569,"title":"How do Garou Families work?","content":"So, a Garou gets pregnant..then what? does she can still fight? is it seen as a &quot;Weakling who keeps the pack behind&quot;? where can i find more info about this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T20:17:33-07:00","id":987578,"title":"","content":"For the first few months, she can continue on as normal, but eventually she'll need to stop fighting (and stay in her breed form) for the sake of the child.<br /> <br /> Garou culture celebrates motherhood despite the removal of a combatant from the front lines, because she's going to give birth to either a kin or a Garou to help ensure the future of the Garou people. She'll earn Renown, not scorn, for it.<br /> <br /> That said, as presented, purposeful pregnancies are usually a higher Rank thing, as the higher Ranks have more roles in their society that are easier to mesh with pregnancy by working primarily at a Sept instead of going out on missions. Also higher Rank makes Rage easier to cheap in check, which makes child rearing easier.<br /> <br /> Actual family life is a different matter. Most of the Tribes have set up ways for children to be raised by kin instead. Some Garou mothers try to be active in their children's lives, but it's a difficult thing to balance. There's a bit of variance by edition as different editions handle knowing which kids will turn into Garou or not. W20 defaults to Garou not having any reliable way to know.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T20:22:35-07:00","id":987580,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms is right. many garou mothers make a point of ritually giving up their children so their safer.<br /> <br /> on a related issue, the black furies had &quot;the rite of freeing the wayward child&quot; in the revised black fury tribe book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T21:46:51-07:00","id":987599,"title":"","content":"call me insensitive basterd but, if the pregnancy was Terminated by any given way, would the garou loose renown? and i dont just mean the scenario where the garou knows she is with Metis and decides to loose it, but in case she gets injured during combat and looses the unborn child?.<br /> <br /> and what happends if a garou ends up sterile due to combat, is it seen as a &quot;Shame&quot; in the garou community or is it treated with some level of empathy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T23:38:07-07:00","id":987643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=987599#post987599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">call me insensitive basterd but, if the pregnancy was Terminated by any given way, would the garou loose renown? and i dont just mean the scenario where the garou knows she is with Metis and decides to loose it, but in case she gets injured during combat and looses the unborn child?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't that depend wholly on how the child was lost...? If a female Garou was foolish and running around and fighting during the final portion of her pregnancy and/or transforming into Crinos unnecessarily, that would likely be a sign there was something wrong with her. I don't know about a renown loss, but her packmates would likely stop her from coming with them.<br /> <br /> If the child died by accident, I doubt the Elders would punish that, unless you want your Garou NPCs to act like total assholes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-15-2016, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T00:22:31-07:00","id":987654,"title":"","content":"There would probably be some Renown loss for an abortion unless there was compelling reasons (such as potentially problematic other parent), since the Garou generally want more in the next generation; not less. That's why all of them end up rationalizing ways to keep the Metis around. They need the numbers.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that the natural health of Garou basically means that all but the most extreme or direct injuries are going to lead to a miscarriage.<br /> <br /> Sterility is generally something of a shame in Garou society, but not to any major degree (there's a Flaw for it). A Battle Scar would generally not carry lasting social consequences because it would be a sign of sacrifice in war for Gaia (though one would imagine a Garou looking at such a wound would be very adamant about having someone with Mother's Touch heal the wound before it can become permanent rather than keeping the Battle Scar for the Glory).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:28:29-07:00","id":987765,"title":"","content":"It is also worth noting that at least 1 Garou was born on a battlefield (Gol-Gol) so fighting while pregnant is at least something that's happened. Granted, it's the Get, so that isn't wholly surprising.<br /> <br /> Other aspects have been covered above. Intentionally terminating a pregnancy shouldn't go over well with Garou (outside of a potential Metis, which has it's own issues) and I would say result in some renown loss. Otherwise, I can't see a potential mother being punished further after losing her child, asumsing it wasn't due to gross negligence.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T10:33:33-07:00","id":987822,"title":"","content":"I would think that a lot of Garou mothers tend to be involved in the lives of their biological children, probably in the form of an 'aunt' or 'older sister', depending on the age difference (I imagine that Garou encourage teenage pregnancy rather than discouraging teenage pregnancy, as the faster a Garou breeds, the sooner a new Garou/Kinfolk is born). I would think that the biological mother will probably reveal her true relationship when her biological child becomes an adult, just to prevent any potential confusion, as genetic attraction can cause as many problems for Garou/Kinfolk as it causes for mundane humans (the normal excuse of 'I was too young/too irresponsible' would probably be used for Kinfolk children while 'I was protecting Gaia' would probably be used for Garou children). In any case, any child of a Garou mother will likely be cherished and protected, as much as possible within the culture of their Tribe, as the Garou are rare (and the Kinfolk are uncommon) and as Garou mothers would likely be capable and willing to killing anyone who harmed their biological children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T13:20:30-07:00","id":987905,"title":"","content":"I can't see the Garou encouraging teen pregnancy.<br /> <br /> If the mother hasn't undergone her first change, you do not want that to happen from the physical trauma of childbirth or the mental stress of child rearing/giving the child up to relatives. It's a recipe for the kind of emotional situations that can lead to a change and put the baby as well as others at risk.<br /> <br /> If the mother had undergone her first change, she's still very new to being a werewolf and keeping her Rage in check. While less a problem than a first change, Frenzy is something that Garou want to avoid in general, and something that takes time for them to get under some semblance of control. <br /> <br /> Some Tribes have better indoctrination methods that could alleviate this, but Garou have strong instincts and you really don't need parenting to add a whole set of instincts, drives, and emotions on an already unstable time in a Garou's life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T20:08:50-07:00","id":988080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=987905#post987905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see the Garou encouraging teen pregnancy.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Some Tribes have better indoctrination methods that could alleviate this, but Garou have strong instincts and you really don't need parenting to add a whole set of instincts, drives, and emotions on an already unstable time in a Garou's life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. 'Teenage Mom Werewolf edition' might make for an interesting (and potentially tragic) story, but I highly doubt that would be a normative occurrence in Garou culture.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T15:42:19-07:00","id":992595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=988080#post988080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. 'Teenage Mom Werewolf edition' might make for an interesting (and potentially tragic) story, but I highly doubt that would be a normative occurrence in Garou culture.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I 100% Agree though I could see one or two tribe breeding kinfolk from an early age.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T17:20:53-07:00","id":992645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=992595#post992595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I 100% Agree though I could see one or two tribe breeding kinfolk from an early age.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but only if you want one or two of your tribes' 'hats' to be 'squick.' A misguided elder or sept might try to enforce a teen or pre-teen breeding program but those are likely the ones who have given into desperation as the Apocalypse looms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T17:37:50-07:00","id":992650,"title":"","content":"I dislike seeing the game become too PC, but I'd agree nonetheless.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another family issue id like to ask about.<br /> <br /> ideas how garou avoid frenzy in a family situation?<br /> <br /> On intimidate, was just curious do I need to add to the difficulty to deliberately pull my punches.<br /> <br /> as I want an intractable kin &quot;Scared, but not too scared&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T17:55:37-07:00","id":992655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=992650#post992650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ideas how garou avoid frenzy in a family situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either:<br /> <br /> 1. Only go near the Kin when it's time to breed, and let the Kin communally raise and rear the kids, or...<br /> <br /> 2. They don't. (Which is why dead Kin are not exactly uncommon).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T18:26:00-07:00","id":992666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=992655#post992655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either:<br /> <br /> 1. Only go near the Kin when it's time to breed, and let the Kin communally raise and rear the kids, or...<br /> <br /> 2. They don't. (Which is why dead Kin are not exactly uncommon).</div> </div> </div> </div>These.<br /> Though on number 1, outside of breeding I do see Garou spending time with their kin, but it really does have to be infrequent to hope to avoid &quot;accidents&quot; (which are generally deadly to kinfolk).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T18:41:10-07:00","id":992670,"title":"","content":"would it be seen as abuse of Gaias gifts or a privilige of rank for an anthro to use &quot;Bury the wolf&quot; to go on a family outing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T20:58:36-07:00","id":992745,"title":"","content":"I think that any Garou with relatively low Rage (3-) and relatively high Willpower (7+) should be safe enough to be around the Kinfolk. The higher the Rage and the lower the Willpower, things get progressively more dangerous for the Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T07:59:30-07:00","id":992947,"title":"","content":"There are also gifts preventing frenzy or shift the rage roll difficulties, so it becomes harder to frenzy.<br /> <br /> In any given case, kin probably shouldn't be around when it is Full Moon and the difficulties are as low as 4. But, that's the time of the month when garou meet up for Moots anyway. Not that it seems particularly clever for all cholerics to meet up, when they are most agitated, but that's the setting.<br /> So, coming together at new moon, makes the whole process that much safer. And it also happens, when you avoid frenzy triggers. Just don't mock the garou guest, neither humiliate him or her. Also, keep well fed so the frenzy difficulty won't change out of your favour again.<br /> <br /> Last, the trigger that is listed with &quot;any strong emotion&quot;, well, that makes coitus without frenzy a difficult endeavour, but there is one big thing most people forget.<br /> A garou doesn't have to frenzy. A single Willpower point makes the whole successes on rage roll mood.<br /> <br /> So, dead kin by raging garou, it happens. But it is by no means common.<br /> <br /> I mean a ST can be a dick and ask for Rage rolls every five minutes, but why?<br /> Is he trying to convey the point that the garou should keep more distant from his/her kin family?<br /> Doesn't he have a plot planned and therefore pushes the frenzy killing family angle to generate drama ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T08:14:54-07:00","id":992954,"title":"","content":"Unless I am missing something, can't a Garou just burn willpower to not rip their spouse/child apart and exit the situation? The threat of frenzy is a problem, but not one that merits complete in-absentia parenting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T11:10:17-07:00","id":993021,"title":"","content":"Yes, though WP is a finite (if renewable) resource that parenting will tax on normal humans without the &quot;don't Frenzy tax.&quot; Not getting any WP regain from getting good sleep, and bleeding WP to resist Frenzies is a great way to end up with dead kin because it isn't sustainable.<br /> <br /> The characters also don't know their Willpower ratings/scores in a numerical sense. A Garou with 1 WP left just knows they're already mentally taxed to close to their limit but could push themselves if they had to, they aren't inherently conscious of having exactly one current Frenzy they can shut down before they flip out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T11:30:07-07:00","id":993028,"title":"","content":"I think that it should be any strong negative emotion (only fear, anger, and hatred) or else you have Garou going into frenzy when they feel happy, loved, proud, etc. Anyway, if Garou were in the habit of experiencing frenzy during sex, the Garou would have gone extinct hundreds of centuries ago, since the probability of a successful conception is only 2.5% (and of a successful pregnancy is only 50% of that). I think that Garou would have been unable to survive if they killed four hundred mates for every Garou child that they produced. If you played it as every strong emotion, positive or negative, you would end up with Werewolf: the Serial Killer rather than Werewolf: the Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:12:59-07:00","id":993095,"title":"","content":"One of the consequences of Apocalypse not having Variable frenzy difficulty, like Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:42:00-07:00","id":993174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=993028#post993028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it should be any strong negative emotion (only fear, anger, and hatred) or else you have Garou going into frenzy when they feel happy, loved, proud, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it should be &quot;negative,&quot; but something that keys into the &quot;fight/flight&quot; reaction. Of course a lot of emotions are mixed anyway. You can't be humiliated without having pride. You can't have grief without having love.<br /> <br /> There definitely should be situations where &quot;positive&quot; emotions are the source of a Frenzy check. A Garou might not care enough to flip out watching a kid get bullied, but should have to check if their child is being bullied; yes you can call that &quot;anger&quot; but it's also love that's the real deciding factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=993095#post993095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the consequences of Apocalypse not having Variable frenzy difficulty, like Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the difficulty is variable, just not variable based on the source of the Frenzy check.<br /> <br /> As well, there is a place for modifying the roll due to situation. You gain temporary Rage even in excess of your permanent Rage, which becomes your dice pool for the roll. And lots of situations that inspire Frenzy checks also risk excess Rage.<br /> <br /> It's kind of a messy mechanic, but it does work to have both the moon-phase impact Frenzy to justify the &quot;full moon brings out werewolves&quot; myth in-universe, and situational Frenzy odds increases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T17:47:57-07:00","id":994303,"title":"","content":"oh on the whole Frenzy thing? Is it unreasonable that a Garou who wants to AVOID Frenzy may actualy learn how to be scarier through mundane means, so that any attempt to intimidate anyone, including a child whos misbehaving, doesnt risk a frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T21:04:49-07:00","id":994392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=994303#post994303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh on the whole Frenzy thing? Is it unreasonable that a Garou who wants to AVOID Frenzy may actualy learn how to be scarier through mundane means, so that any attempt to intimidate anyone, including a child whos misbehaving, doesnt risk a frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not really. Though I personally feel like that errs a bit too much on the out-of-game system knowledge of the roll. It is at the very least a gray area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T21:59:39-07:00","id":994403,"title":"","content":"that is a mechanical thing I would like a way to explain the mechanics in universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T23:19:00-07:00","id":994427,"title":"","content":"How does having high Intimidation help you avoid frenzy just because you're good at scaring people without the aid of your Rage?<br /> <br /> It's not mind control. And it's a shitty way to raise a child if you expect them to actually behave. Being psychologically abusive beyond what a Garou can't exactly help by virtue of what they are, is just going to increase the odds of misbehavior, parental frustration, and thus Frenzy.<br /> <br /> If a Garou's child is in the midst of the terrible twos, even if you're so scary you can just them up with a glare, doesn't mean you're free from Frenzy from all the stuff they do that makes you want to intimidate them into stopping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T00:55:02-07:00","id":994456,"title":"","content":"High Intimidation is working in homid form, while being in Crinos causes a modifier to the Frenzy Difficulty, iirc. So learning how to intimidate without the need to shapeshift can prevent frenzy.<br /> <br /> While certainly caring for a newborn or toddler can be exhausting, and the parents condition can be similar to being tortured, I still think that garou wouldn't kill their own children. Yes, Willpower is a finite, but renewable resource, but Rage is too. And if you have neither, you can't regain Rage, shape shift or frenzy. So, being exhausted basically can be the reason the whole thing works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T03:28:13-07:00","id":994481,"title":"","content":"Intimidation works in any form (though form modifiers influence which applications are worth using). Yes Crinos makes Frenzy rolls worse, but why on Earth would you be shifting to Crinos to scold your child? If you have to shift to chastise a kin... you're doing something wrong long before that point (also... the loss of clear human language communication skills is going to be an issue).<br /> <br /> And I'm not trying to say that Garou regularly Frenzy and kill their own children, but that the books' portrayal of the Garou as generally leaving parenting to the kin until a First Change happens is consistent with how the rules play out: it's much, much safer for everyone involved for the Garou to be hands-off parents.<br /> <br /> And that includes losing the wolf, since that's an incredibly weak state to be in and it means the Garou in question is in no position to do things like protect their family or perform their duties as warriors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T04:31:03-07:00","id":994492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=994481#post994481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm not trying to say that Garou regularly Frenzy and kill their own children, but that the books' portrayal of the Garou as generally leaving parenting to the kin until a First Change happens is consistent with how the rules play out: it's much, much safer for everyone involved for the Garou to be hands-off parents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this is the usual way to go.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T05:10:16-07:00","id":994501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=994427#post994427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does having high Intimidation help you avoid frenzy just because you're good at scaring people without the aid of your Rage?<br /> <br /> It's not mind control. And it's a shitty way to raise a child if you expect them to actually behave. Being psychologically abusive beyond what a Garou can't exactly help by virtue of what they are, is just going to increase the odds of misbehavior, parental frustration, and thus Frenzy.<br /> <br /> If a Garou's child is in the midst of the terrible twos, even if you're so scary you can just them up with a glare, doesn't mean you're free from Frenzy from all the stuff they do that makes you want to intimidate them into stopping.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because if your rage is higher then your Man + Intimidate dice pool, you roll that instead and if you get more then 3 successes you enter frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T06:38:10-07:00","id":994535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=994501#post994501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if your rage is higher then your Man + Intimidate dice pool, you roll that instead and if you get more then 3 successes you enter frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Garou who goes around deliberately Intimidating Kinfolk is just asking to get skinned anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T06:48:44-07:00","id":994538,"title":"","content":"&quot;Goes around&quot; doing so yes.<br /> <br /> but &quot;impressing on someone their position&quot; Is something someone may do every other day without realizing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:56:16-07:00","id":994868,"title":"","content":"If the ST if forcing you to roll Intimidation checks/Rage if its higher... I think that's a very different issue.<br /> <br /> Using the Intimidation Ability should be a purposeful choice for the character, and Garou aren't going to default to Intimidation against kin as a first, second, or third option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:34:34-07:00","id":994896,"title":"","content":"Kinfolk already know they are support rather than combat, reserve rather than active, so I doubt any Garou needs to prove anything. If an individual Kinfolk starts trying to show up Garou, well, I imagine the local Garou will invite him on fomori hunts until he dies, learns his lesson, or proves his worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:47:15-07:00","id":994907,"title":"","content":"its in the 3rd edition corebobok a short story under the Appearance attribute, Thea (from kinfolk unsung heroes) Wanted to go to a party her b ro ther Ian Puts her in her place with a glare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T17:51:55-07:00","id":994980,"title":"","content":"So Ian's an idiot that ignores what the Garou consider common sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T18:39:42-07:00","id":994992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987569-how-do-garou-families-work?p=994980#post994980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Ian's an idiot that ignores what the Garou consider common sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if he found out about that time Thea met with that BSD kin woman...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:01:50-07:00","id":995000,"title":"","content":"... Thea and Ian have a lot bigger problems on their hands than her going to a club?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T21:14:55-07:00","id":995063,"title":"","content":"Not quite. Thea was researching how Kin in other tribes relate to their Garou relatives. For the sake of completeness, she sought out a Dancer Kin to get her take on the tribe. She (Thea) later opined that Ian Gleam-In-His-Eye would take a <i>very</i> dim view if he ever found out. (Which would be why she, other Kin, and even at least one Garou, were taking precautions that he <i>didn't</i>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T04:54:58-07:00","id":995154,"title":"","content":"I remember her commenting that she wouldnt be allowed out unchaperogned until she was 60, or was it 50... dont remember.<br /> <br /> Oh just thought Could Ian get Thea Microchipped?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"